<section id="built" class="fade-in scroll-mt-24">
  <h2 class="mb-2 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-white">Built with AI</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-sm text-slate">Proof I know AI deeply — I build the tooling, not just use it.</p>
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <div class="glass-card p-6">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Agentes Hub</h3>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-accent shrink-0">97.5% token savings</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-light">
        A multi-agent system that automates code review — security, performance, quality and architecture
        agents running in parallel, across Claude, OpenAI and Gemini.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="tech-tag">TypeScript</span><span class="tech-tag">LangChain</span><span class="tech-tag">Multi-LLM</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card p-6">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">ContextForge</h3>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate shrink-0">Rust · MCP</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-light">
        An MCP server giving AI coding assistants persistent semantic memory — hybrid keyword + vector search,
        code intelligence across 50+ languages, in a single Rust binary.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="tech-tag">Rust</span><span class="tech-tag">Vector search</span><span class="tech-tag">MCP</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card p-6">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Claude Statusline</h3>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-slate shrink-0">npm</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-light">
        A real-time statusline for the Claude Code CLI — context usage, rate limits and git state,
        rendered in under 50ms. Published on npm.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="tech-tag">Node.js</span><span class="tech-tag">CLI</span><span class="tech-tag">npm</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="glass-card border-l-2 border-accent/40 p-6 text-center">
      <h3 class="font-semibold text-white">Try the AI Playground — live in your browser</h3>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-2 max-w-md text-sm text-slate-light">
        Sentiment, RAG, summarization, speech-to-text and image models running client-side.
        <span class="text-white">The chat button in the corner is one of them.</span>
        The kind of AI-product feature I drop into real products.
      </p>
      <a href="/playground" class="mt-4 inline-block rounded-lg border border-accent/30 bg-accent/10 px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent transition hover:bg-accent/20">Try the playground →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-5 text-center">
    <a href="/projects" class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-slate transition-colors hover:text-accent">See all projects →</a>
  </p>
</section>
